<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Random Picture Picker | Choose From Your Images</title><meta name="description" content="Select images from your device and randomly choose one. Images stay in your browser session and are not uploaded by this tool."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="https://wheelnamepicker.com.au/picture-picker"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/value-pages.css"></head><body><div class="top"><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Wheel Name Picker</a><div class="links"><a href="/colour-picker">Colour Picker</a><a href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker</a><a href="/student-picker">Student Picker</a></div></div></div><header class="hero"><span class="badge">Visual choice tool</span><h1>Random Picture Picker</h1><p>Select several images from your device, preview the available choices and let the page pick one at random. The selected files remain local to this browser session.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="tool"><div class="field"><label for="files">Choose images</label><input id="files" type="file" accept="image/*" multiple></div><div class="actions"><button id="pick">Pick a picture</button><button class="secondary" id="clear">Clear pictures</button></div><div class="result" id="result">Choose at least two images to begin.</div><div class="preview" id="preview"></div></div><div class="article"><section><h2>A visual alternative to a name list</h2><p>Some choices are easier to recognise as pictures than words. A picture picker can work well for young children, visual classroom prompts, craft references, meal photos, activity cards or any set of options that is already stored as images.</p></section><section><h2>What happens to the files?</h2><p>The page reads the selected images inside your browser so it can display previews and choose one. This tool does not require an account and its JavaScript does not intentionally upload those selected files to a server. Reloading or leaving the page clears the current selection.</p><p class="note">Avoid using sensitive images on a shared or public device, and follow your organisation's privacy rules for photographs of children or other people.</p></section><section><h2>Ways to use a picture picker</h2><ul><li>Choose between photos of several craft ideas.</li><li>Let a child pick from visual activity cards without needing to read each option.</li><li>Select a reference image for a drawing warm-up.</li><li>Choose one of several meal photos when deciding what to make.</li><li>Pick a flashcard image for an informal learning game.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Keep the set manageable</h2><p>Large high-resolution images can use a lot of device memory because the browser has to hold previews during the session. For a quick choice, a small set of ordinary phone photos or compressed images works best. If the page becomes sluggish, clear the pictures and select fewer or smaller files.</p></section><section><h2>Random selection is only the final step</h2><p>Make sure every image in the pool is genuinely acceptable before pressing pick. If some activities are unsuitable because of time, weather, cost or safety, remove those images first. The picker cannot evaluate the content of the photographs.</p></section></div></main><footer class="footer"><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><p>© 2026 Wheel Name Picker · Ascension Digital Group</p></footer><script>const input=document.getElementById('files'),result=document.getElementById('result'),preview=document.getElementById('preview');let items=[];function cleanup(){items.forEach(x=>URL.revokeObjectURL(x.url));items=[];preview.innerHTML='';result.textContent='Choose at least two images to begin.';input.value=''}input.onchange=()=>{items.forEach(x=>URL.revokeObjectURL(x.url));items=[...input.files].map(f=>({name:f.name,url:URL.createObjectURL(f)}));preview.innerHTML=items.map(x=>`<img src="${x.url}" alt="Selected image ${x.name.replace(/[<>]/g,'')}">`).join('');result.textContent=items.length?`${items.length} picture${items.length===1?'':'s'} ready.`:'Choose at least two images to begin.'};document.getElementById('pick').onclick=()=>{if(!items.length)return result.textContent='Choose at least one image.';const x=items[Math.floor(Math.random()*items.length)];result.innerHTML=`<div class="preview"><img src="${x.url}" alt="Randomly selected picture"><div><strong>${x.name.replace(/[<>]/g,'')}</strong><br>Selected from ${items.length} picture${items.length===1?'':'s'}.</div></div>`};document.getElementById('clear').onclick=cleanup;window.addEventListener('beforeunload',()=>items.forEach(x=>URL.revokeObjectURL(x.url)));</script></body></html>